offs. While some find them repugnant, others note that they=E2=80=99ve prov=
ided an entry point for new enthusiasts and collectors. A Reddit group for =
enthusiasts has doubled to ~368k users over the past five years.<br><br>Art=
ist and enthusiast Irv Tepper, who boasts a collection of 200+ pens, told <=
em>WSJ</em> he actually prefers the cheaper Chinese-made pens for everyday =
use and to gift to people he hopes to introduce to his hobby. <br><br><span=
 style=3D"font-weight: bold; font-size: 18px;">Are there similar trends?&nb=
sp;</span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><br>As our lives have become increasingly dig=
itized, there=E2=80=99s been a rising interest in physical media (vinyl rec=
ords, cassette tapes, board games, etc.) and hobbies that involve using you=
r hands or getting outdoors.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold"><br><span style=3D"font-wei=
ght: normal;">There=E2=80=99s also been a growing demand for stationery, a =
